    <innernamespace refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk_1_1Pdu">OpenSkyhawk::Pdu</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>PDU per-board calibration in a reserved flash page — append-only log, newest valid wins (#216). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The F103 has no EEPROM, so calibration lives in the last 1 KB flash page (PDU_CAL_PAGE_ADDR), outside the firmware image: the PDU builds set <computeroutput>board_upload.maximum_size = 64512</computeroutput> so the build fails before code can grow into it, and an OpenOCD upload erases only the sectors it writes, so a reflash keeps the calibration.</para>
<para>The page holds up to 32 fixed 32-byte records. save() writes the next empty slot; load() returns the last slot whose magic and CRC check out. The page is erased only when it is full, so a power cut can lose at most the record being written — never the previous good one — except during the rare full-page erase.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
